#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:83
msgid ""
"The ``version`` supports `Semantic Versioning <https://devhints.io/semver>`_ "
"( ``<major>.<minor>.<patch>``) and can take any of the following forms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:86
msgid ""
"``^1.2.3`` - any compatible version (new functionality in a backwards "
"compatible manner and patches are allowed, 1.x.x). **RECOMMENDED**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:87
msgid ""
"``~1.2.3`` - any version with the same major and minor versions, and an "
"equal or greater patch version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:89
msgid ""
"``>1.2.3`` - any version greater than ``1.2.3``. ``>=``, ``<``, and ``<=`` "
"are also possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:91
msgid ""
"``>0.1.0,!=0.2.0,<0.3.0`` - any version greater than ``0.1.0``, not equal to "
"``0.2.0`` and less than ``0.3.0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:93
msgid "``1.2.3`` - an exact version number. Use only this exact version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/platforms/cmd_install.rst:95
msgid ""
"Also, PlatformIO supports installing from local directory or archive. Need "
